ur transmembrane spans, with cytosolic amino- and carboxy-termini. DMP1 is a membrane protein that may be involved in membrane fission during breakdown of the ER and the tonoplast during leaf senescence and in membrane fusion during vacuole biogenesis in roots [[cite:PUB00086645]]. Several DMP proteins are expressed in senescing organs (DMP1, -3, -4) or tissues that will stall later in development (DMP1, -2, -4, -7). These expression patterns strongly suggest involvement of several DMPs in various programmed cell death processes, e.g. senescence, dehiscence and abscission [[cite:PUB00136742]]. AtDMP8 and AtDMP9 however, have been shown to facilitate gamete fusion during double fertilisation in flowering plants [[cite:PUB00093467]].","domain_architectures":52,"interpro_id":"IPR007770","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":4715,"name":"Protein of unknown function (DUF679)","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF05078","proteins":4584,"proteomes":395,"short_name":"DUF679","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF05078","structures":0,"taxa":1097,"unknown_status":"UNKNOWN_CANDIDATE"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-direct-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"SEEDED","local_source":"source/data/families/PF05078.yaml","record":{"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":3757,"domain_architectures":52,"matches":4715,"proteins":4584,"proteomes":395,"structures":0,"taxa":1097},"curation_status":"SEEDED","description":"This family includes members such as plant proteins AtDMPs 1-10 (Arabidopsis thaliana DUF679 domain membrane proteins 1 -10) [[cite:PUB00136742]]. The AtDMP proteins are predicted to have four transmembrane spans, with cytosolic amino- and carboxy-termini. DMP1 is a membrane protein that may be involved in membrane fission during breakdown of the ER and the tonoplast during leaf senescence and in membrane fusion during vacuole biogenesis in roots [[cite:PUB00086645]]. Several DMP proteins are expressed in senescing organs (DMP1, -3, -4) or tissues that will stall later in development (DMP1, -2, -4, -7). These expression patterns strongly suggest involvement of several DMPs in various programmed cell death processes, e.g. senescence, dehiscence and abscission [[cite:PUB00136742]]. AtDMP8 and AtDMP9 however, have been shown to facilitate gamete fusion during double fertilisation in flowering plants [[cite:PUB00093467]].","id":"Pfam:PF05078","interpro_id":"InterPro:IPR007770","name":"Protein of unknown function (DUF679)","pfam_id":"PF05078","provenance":{"generated_at":"2026-10-10T07:44:21.614711Z","path":"data/worklists/interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10.json","sha256":"17fb625876c9326ed284263a47bcd84e0d7844a31c040dc06cd2260c36f1c383","snapshot_id":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/"},"seed_status":"UNKNOWN_CANDIDATE","short_name":"DUF679","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF05078"},"source":{"commit":"a813667bafdf952818dfe781facff3af5369d83e","path":"data/families/PF05078.yaml","repository":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/DUFMech","sha256":"b355c9df4596b091eeb00189343ef47009dccbe98e4a2ea5a963ea1dfe10f797"}},"protein_examples":{"candidate_count":7,"discovery_scanned":true,"example_count":7,"examples":[{"evidence_scope":"FAMILY_MEMBERSHIP_NOT_FUNCTION","organism":"Arabidopsis thaliana","origins":[{"cited_uniprot_accession":"","commit":"70edd6f8458845f7d7783ac4f416df519f5e1de6","link_basis":["canonical_example_family_classification"],"mech":"ProteinTraitsMech","path":"data/traits/function/pathway/go/fusion-of-sperm-to-egg-plasma-membrane-involved-in-double-fertilization-forming--go0061936.yaml","qualification_status":"NOT_ASSESSED","record_id":"GO:0061936","section":"canonical_examples","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/pr